# Importing from Lovable

Lovable owns the design. The Lovable project uses the **exact same design tokens**
as this repo (`src/styles.css` there == `src/app/globals.css` here: same oklch
colors, spacing, radius, text tokens). So the visual layer transfers **1:1**.

Lovable project id: `c518057a-e525-4963-8ead-f4a5e3f535b9`. Read the real source
with the Lovable MCP (`list_files`, `read_file`) — never reconstruct a screen from a
screenshot or memory.

## Import completeness — do NOT skip parts

A single "page" in Lovable is almost always a **cluster** of route files + child
components, not one file. Skipping happens when you port only the main screen and
rebuild the rest from memory. Prevent it with this process, every time:

1. **Inventory first.** `list_files` on the Lovable project and list EVERY file that
   belongs to the feature before writing any code:
   - the layout route (holds tab menus/nav) and ALL of its child routes
     (`.index`, `.new`, `.settings`, `.dashboard`, `.$id`, nested `tasks.*`, etc.)
   - every component imported by those routes (cards, dialogs, pickers, chips, sheets)
2. **Make a checklist** (use a todo list) with one item per route AND per component.
   Nothing gets marked done until its file is actually ported.
3. **Read each file with `read_file` and port it 1:1.** Don't summarize, don't merge,
   don't drop dialogs/empty-states/menus.
4. **Verify at the end**: re-list the feature's Lovable files and confirm every one has
   a Falak counterpart. Report anything intentionally skipped.

### Example: the "project" feature is 9 routes + ~9 components
Routes: `projects.index`, `projects.new`, `projects.$projectId` (tab menu/layout),
`projects.$projectId.index`, `projects.$projectId.dashboard`, `projects.$projectId.assets`,
`projects.$projectId.settings`, `projects.$projectId.tasks.new`,
`projects.$projectId.tasks.$taskId`.
Components: `board/task-card`, `board/confirm-status-dialog`, `board/decline-dialog`,
`projects/dynamic-field`, `projects/priority-picker`, `projects/task-type-chip`,
`surface-card`, `task-type-visuals`, `add-item-input`.
Porting only the board = skipping the tab menu, settings page, create-task page, and card design.

## Golden rule: keep every Tailwind class verbatim

Do **NOT** rewrite Lovable's utility classes. Copy them exactly as-is:

- Keep colors/semantic classes (`bg-card`, `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-primary`, `border-border`) — identical tokens exist here.
- Keep sizes exactly (`h-9`, `w-4 h-4`, `px-3`, `gap-2`, `rounded-lg`).
- Keep breakpoints exactly (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`). Lovable uses viewport breakpoints and they work.
- Keep spacing tokens (`p-card-pad`, `gap-section-gap`), radius (`rounded-card`), and text tokens (`text-label`, `text-hint`, `text-xxs`, `text-tiny`) — all defined in `globals.css`.
- Keep component structure, hierarchy, animations, gradients, shadows.

Do **NOT** convert classes to `text-body` / `min-h-touch` / `w-icon-sm` / `h-input` /
`@md:` / `cq-adapt`. Those tokens are **not defined** in `globals.css`, so they render
as no-ops and will visually break the imported design. (See note below.)

## What to actually change: the framework layer only

The Lovable project is **TanStack Start**; this repo is **Next.js App Router**.
Only rewire the plumbing:

### Routing
| Lovable (TanStack Start) | Falak (Next.js) |
|---|---|
| `src/routes/foo.tsx` | `src/app/foo/page.tsx` |
| `src/routes/projects.$projectId.tsx` | `src/app/(dashboard)/projects/[projectId]/page.tsx` |
| `src/routes/projects.$projectId.tasks.$taskId.tsx` | `.../projects/[projectId]/tasks/[taskId]/page.tsx` |
| `src/routes/__root.tsx` | `src/app/layout.tsx` + `(dashboard)/layout.tsx` |
| `src/routes/login.tsx` | Clerk sign-in route |

### Navigation & params
| Lovable (`@tanstack/react-router`) | Falak (`next/*`) |
|---|---|
| `import { Link } from "@tanstack/react-router"` | `import Link from "next/link"` (use `href=`) |
| `useNavigate()` | `useRouter()` from `next/navigation` |
| `useParams()` | `useParams()` from `next/navigation` |

### Data
- Replace zustand stores that hold **server data** (`src/lib/*-store.ts`) and mock data (`src/components/home/data.ts`) with **server actions** from `src/actions/` backed by Prisma.
- Pure UI/client state (open/closed, drafts) may stay as zustand — this repo uses zustand too.

### Server vs client
- Data-fetching pages → keep as **server components**, fetch via server actions/Prisma.
- Interactive pieces (state, effects, event handlers) → add `"use client"` at the top.

### Reuse existing infra
- Use existing shared components where equivalents exist.
- Integrate Clerk auth where the Lovable route assumed a logged-in user.

## Note: don't invent tokens that don't exist

Tokens like `text-body`, `min-h-touch`, `w-icon-sm`, `h-input`, `@md:`, and `cq-adapt`
are **not defined** in `globals.css` and there is no Tailwind config, so those classes
render as no-ops. Always use the raw Tailwind classes Lovable outputs (`h-9`, `w-4 h-4`,
`md:`, etc.) plus the semantic tokens that *are* defined in `globals.css`
(`bg-card`, `text-muted-foreground`, `p-card-pad`, `rounded-card`, `text-label`).
